---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="About this starter" description="How to adapt the reusable website starter.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h1>A starting point, not a locked-in design.</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">This repository is being built as a reusable website foundation. It separates editable content from shared page structure so each new client project can begin with a sensible baseline.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="template-grid">
        <article class="template-card"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Update the content</h3><p>Start with src/content/site.ts and replace the sample brand details with the real project brief.</p></article>
        <article class="template-card"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Choose a template</h3><p>Open a starter page under /templates/ and adapt its copy and sections to the client's goals.</p></article>
        <article class="template-card"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Build and review</h3><p>Run the production build, check mobile layouts, and review links and metadata before deployment.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
